{"Title":"An Act to promote fairness between traditional public schools and regional vocational schools","BillNumber":"H485","DocketNumber":"HD1337","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:10:24.367"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:10:24.3666667"},{"Id":"NJO1","Name":"Norman J. Orrall","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/NJO1","ResponseDate":"2023-04-06T12:49:32.6666667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H485/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Garry of Dracut, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 485) of Colleen M. Garry for legislation to establish parity in funding for regional vocational school districts and traditional public school districts.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding the provisions of section 6 of Chapter 70 of the General laws, no regional vocational school district shall receive an annual contribution from a member municipality greater than the percentage increase appropriated for the member’s traditional public school district’s annual budget percentage increase.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}